# Faidlix Blender Add-on Distribution

- Keep every add-on under `addons/<AddonName>/` on `main`; never use branches as add-on categories.
- Each add-on must have its own manifest, package ID, version, README, tests, and buildable ZIP.
- Add-ons must remain independently installable, updateable, disableable, and removable.
- Never import another Faidlix add-on or require `faidlix_manager` at runtime.
- Use `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Faidlix/BlenderAddons/main/repository/index.json` for online updates.
- Put release ZIP files in `repository/` and keep only the latest ZIP for each package ID.
- `faidlix_manager` may update installed packages only; it must never install unselected add-ons.
- Preserve the package ID and bump the version when migrating an existing add-on.
- Publish one migration release through the old repository before retiring its update path.
- Every completed add-on change, for **every** package under `addons/`, must be treated as a release: bump its version, test source in Blender, build and validate its ZIP/index/README, commit and push GitHub, read back the remote commit and ZIP checksum, then install that GitHub ZIP into the formal Blender environment and verify the installed version/files. Local-only packaging or an isolated test install is not completion.
- Before replacing a formal installation, check whether Blender has unsaved work or is using that add-on, and back up the existing extension. Never force-close Blender, discard user work, hot-swap an in-use extension, or claim installation succeeded when safety checks, network, or validation block it. Report the exact remaining step and resume when safe.
